Move aws-lc-rs 1.18.1 -> 1.18.2 and with it aws-lc-sys 0.45.0 -> 0.46.0.

jitterentropy must be compiled at -O0. aws-lc-sys 0.45.0 rewrites CFLAGS
to that only after it has created the cc builder for it, and the cc 1.11
in this lockfile snapshots the environment when a builder first reads it,
so the -O2 of a Gentoo CFLAGS reaches jitterentropy-base.c and its #error
stops the build (cc has snapshotted since 1.6.0). 0.46.0 sets the
override before creating the builder (aws/aws-lc-rs#1254, for #1252).

Generated with `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs@1.18.1 --precise 1.18.2` on
top of the RustSec patch.

